      "selected_candidate_id": "impact_claim_accounting_reporting_drift_c462d1fb_4a0b0262::canonical",
      "candidates": [
        {
          "candidate_id": "impact_claim_accounting_reporting_drift_c462d1fb_4a0b0262::canonical",
          "text": "sUSDM.decimals() must equal assetDecimals + _decimalsOffset() (i.e., 12 given USDM's 6 decimals and offset 6), matching ERC-4626 semantics.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "implies",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "eq",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "var": "c72c5b129_expected_decimals"
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "add",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "var": "c72c5b129_asset_decimals"
                      },
                      {
                        "var": "c72c5b129_decimals_offset"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "eq",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "var": "c72c5b129_reported_decimals"
                  },
                  {
                    "var": "c72c5b129_expected_decimals"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "derivation": "canonical_formalization",
          "source_ids": [
            "intent_decimals_matches_offset"
          ],
          "evidence_ids": [
            "Under OpenZeppelin ERC-4626, the vault’s decimals should be:",
            "vaultDecimals=assetDecimals+_decimalsOffset()",
            "USDM uses 6 decimals, so with _decimalsOffset() = 6, ERC-4626 expects sUSDM.decimals() to be 12.",
            "2. OZ ERC-4626 defines decimals() as underlyingDecimals + _decimalsOffset().",
            "- Result: sUSDM.decimals() becomes 12 (given USDM has 6 decimals), matching ERC-4626 semantics."
          ],
          "checkpoints": {
            "raw": {
              "c72c5b129_asset_decimals": "before checked decimals() read",
              "c72c5b129_decimals_offset": "before checked decimals() read",
              "c72c5b129_expected_decimals": "derived from before checked decimals() read",
              "c72c5b129_reported_decimals": "at decimals() read"
            },
            "normalized": {
              "c72c5b129_asset_decimals": "before",
              "c72c5b129_decimals_offset": "before",
              "c72c5b129_expected_decimals": "before",
              "c72c5b129_reported_decimals": "snapshot"
            }
          },
          "quality_labels": [
            "CHECKPOINT_SNAPSHOT_ONLY"
          ],
          "executable": true,
          "score": 3.35
        },
        {
          "candidate_id": "impact_claim_accounting_reporting_drift_c462d1fb_4a0b0262::intent_consistent_share_model",
          "text": "The share token must use one consistent decimals model so that ERC-4626 math and reported share decimals agree.",
          "expression": null,
          "derivation": "explicit_report_intent",
          "source_ids": [
            "intent_consistent_share_model"
          ],
          "evidence_ids": [
            "sUSDM implements ERC-4626 with a non-zero _decimalsOffset() but overrides decimals() to an inconsistent value, causing share-unit mismatches between ERC-4626 math and what integrators/users think the share token decimals are. This can lead to incorrect pricing/quotes, wrong UI display, and unsafe integration behavior for any system relying on ERC-4626 semantics.",
            "its better to just choose one consistent model:",
            "- Result: shares and assets both use 6 decimals, and ERC-4626 semantics stay consistent."
          ],
          "checkpoints": {
            "raw": {},
            "normalized": {
              "report_level": "snapshot"
            }
          },
          "quality_labels": [
            "CANDIDATE_ONLY"
          ],
          "executable": false,
          "score": 1.6
        }
      ]
    },
